    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the Python file that retrieves aggregated statistics for a metric over a time window using an external provider, I need to choose a specific provider and use its API or SDK. For this task, I will use the AWS CloudWatch service, which is a monitoring service for AWS cloud resources and applications. I will import the boto3 library, which is the AWS SDK for Python, to interact with CloudWatch. The code will include the boto3 import and a client for CloudWatch, making the provider identifiable. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789864051592,
          "start": 1789864048208
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc35f650001JQM3W5dwCcPNSe",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc35f2810018iI67ppOOafETV",
      "session_id": "ses_f43ca0d8cffeIZS5I39LNiDB7y",
